    description: "## Problem\n\nStarlette HTTP routes and WebSocket routes are completely invisible to hypergumbo. On hypergumbo's own tracker package (`packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/serve.py`), 7 HTTP routes and 1 WebSocketRoute are defined but produce **0 nodes with `kind=route`** and **0 nodes with `meta.concepts[].concept==\"route\"`** in the behavior map. The 9 handler functions (`_health`, `_api_list_items`, `_api_add_item`, `_api_get_item`, `_api_update_item`, `_api_discuss_item`, `_api_ready`, `_ws_handler`, `_handle_ws_message`) are detected only as bare `function` symbols with no route concepts attached.\n\nThis affects every Starlette codebase. Profile detection correctly identifies `starlette` is in use (`profile.py:72`), but no further extraction follows.\n\n## Layered root cause\n\nThe fix is **not** as simple as adding `frameworks/starlette.yaml`. Three layers must change together:\n\n### Layer 1: No `frameworks/starlette.yaml`\n\nOf ~100 framework YAMLs, none target Starlette specifically. `litestar.yaml` is for the Litestar (formerly Starlite) framework — different idiom, decorator-driven. `fastapi.yaml` matches decorators (`@app.get`) and one usage pattern (`router.add_api_route`).\n\n### Layer 2: The YAML pattern system is downstream of analyzer-emitted UsageContexts\n\n`fastapi.yaml`'s `add_api_route` pattern uses:\n```yaml\n- concept: route\n  usage:\n    kind: \"^call$\"\n    name: \"^(app|router|\\\\w+_router)\\\\.add_api_route$\"\n    position: \"^view_func$\"\n  extract:\n    path: \"metadata.route_path\"\n    method: \"metadata.methods\"\n```\n\nThe `extract:` block reads from `metadata.route_path` / `metadata.methods` — keys that must already exist on a `UsageContext` emitted by the **analyzer** (not by the YAML matcher). The matcher is a join layer; it does not crawl AST itself.\n\n### Layer 3: UsageContext emission for routes is gated by hard-coded allowlists in `py.py`\n\n```python\n# packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/py.py:413\nDJANGO_URL_FUNCTIONS = {\"path\", \"re_path\", \"url\"}\n\n# py.py:422\nFLASK_URL_FUNCTIONS = {\"add_url_rule\", \"add_api_route\", \"add_resource\"}\n```\n\nEach set has a hand-written extractor — `_extract_django_url_patterns` (line ~770) and `_extract_flask_url_patterns` (line ~1180) — that walks the AST, recognizes the call shape, and builds `metadata` with `route_path`, `methods`, `view_name`, `args`. There is no `STARLETTE_ROUTE_FUNCTIONS` set and no `_extract_starlette_route_patterns` function.\n\n## Fix shape\n\nThree coordinated changes in one PR:\n\n1. **`STARLETTE_ROUTE_FUNCTIONS = {\"Route\", \"WebSocketRoute\"}`** added near the existing constants in `py.py:422`. (`Mount` is deferred — see \"Out of scope\".)\n\n2. **`_extract_starlette_route_patterns(...)`** in `py.py`, structurally parallel to `_extract_flask_url_patterns` (~80 LOC). Recognizes:\n   - `Route(\"/path\", handler, methods=[\"GET\", \"POST\"])` → `metadata.route_path` = path, `metadata.methods` = `[\"GET\", \"POST\"]`, `metadata.view_name` = handler name, `metadata.args` per existing convention.\n   - `WebSocketRoute(\"/ws\", handler)` → `metadata.route_path` = path, `metadata.methods` = `[\"WS\"]` (synthetic, conventional for websockets), `metadata.view_name` = handler name.\n   - Wired into the same enrichment loop the Django/Flask extractors run from.\n\n3. **`packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/frameworks/starlette.yaml`** with the usage patterns:\n   ```yaml\n   id: starlette\n   language: python\n   patterns:\n     - concept: route\n       usage:\n         kind: \"^call$\"\n         name: \"^Route$\"\n         position: \"^args\\\\[1\\\\]$\"\n       extract:\n         path: \"metadata.route_path\"\n         method: \"metadata.methods\"\n     - concept: route\n       usage:\n         kind: \"^call$\"\n         name: \"^WebSocketRoute$\"\n         position: \"^args\\\\[1\\\\]$\"\n       extract:\n         path: \"metadata.route_path\"\n         method: \"metadata.methods\"\n   linkers:\n     - http\n     - websocket\n   ```\n\n## Design decision: import-scoped vs. bare class-name match\n\nUnlike `path()` / `add_url_rule()` which are unambiguous function names, `Route` is a common class name. A user repo with its own unrelated `Route` class would otherwise produce FP route symbols.\n\n**Decision: strict / import-scoped match.** Only emit a UsageContext for `Route(...)` if `Route` was imported from `starlette.routing` (or aliased from the same module) in the current file's `imports` dict. The `imports` dict is already threaded into the existing extractors. ~5 extra LOC. Same treatment for `WebSocketRoute`.\n\nThis matches hypergumbo's general bias toward precision in framework dispatch.\n\n## Validation\n\n### Self-analysis (immediate)\n\nAfter the fix, `hypergumbo run .` on hypergumbo's own repo should produce:\n- ≥7 route nodes from `serve.py` (paths: `/health`, `/api/items` ×2, `/api/items/{item_id}`, `/api/items/{item_id}/update`, `/api/items/{item_id}/discuss`, `/api/ready`)\n- ≥1 route node from `serve.py` for `/ws` (WebSocketRoute, method `WS`)\n- `hypergumbo routes` output: 7 routes shown for serve.py\n- 9 handler functions linked from those routes via http linker (Layer 2 includes `linkers: [http, websocket]`).\n\n### Test plan\n\nUnit tests in `packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/`:\n- Fixture: a Python file mirroring `serve.py`'s shape with `Route`/`WebSocketRoute` constructors imported from `starlette.routing`.\n- Assert: ≥7 UsageContexts emitted with `metadata.route_path` populated.\n- Assert: 1 UsageContext for the WebSocketRoute with `metadata.methods == [\"WS\"]`.\n- Negative fixture: a file with a class named `Route` imported from a different module (or defined locally) → 0 route UsageContexts emitted.\n- Integration: load `starlette.yaml`, run the matcher against the fixture's UsageContexts, assert ≥7 route concepts attached.\n\n100% coverage required (existing repo policy).\n\n## Quantitative bakeoff claim — `awaits_bakeoff_validation`\n\nThis PR carries quantitative claims:\n- \"≥7 new route nodes detected on hypergumbo self-analysis\"\n- \"Route detection extends to Starlette repos in the bakeoff corpus, with per-repo route-count deltas\"\n\nThe PR must receive `awaits_bakeoff_validation` at merge time per the bakeoff validation discipline in AGENTS.md. Discharge requires a DEEP cycle whose cohort contains at least one Starlette-using repo. If the current corpus has none, that's a cohort-coverage gap to surface in the validation pass — not a reason to skip the tag.\n\n## Out of scope (filed or to be filed as follow-ups)\n\n- **`Mount(\"/prefix\", app=...)` for nested ASGI apps.** Smaller surface area; defer until a user surfaces the need.\n- **`Starlette(routes=[...])` constructor `routes` kwarg.** The current pattern detects each `Route(...)` call wherever it sits; routes inside a kwarg list are still call expressions in the AST, so they're caught. No additional handling required — verify in tests.\n- **Concept-distinct `websocket_endpoint` for the WebSocketRoute case** (vs. the current `concept=route` with `methods=[\"WS\"]`). This is a downstream classification question that interacts with gap (3); resolve it after observing how downstream commands consume the new metadata.\n\n## Source\n\nSelf-analysis dogfooding session, hypergumbo 3.0.0 @ d5e3941c6, 2026-04-29."  # bcdd
